<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Canton of Glarus</h1><p class="st-meta">1352 CE – 1798 CE · capital Glarus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Alpine valley canton that won its freedom from the Habsburgs at Näfels in 1388 and later divided its government between Catholics and Protestants.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/linth">Linth</a> valley belonged to the abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sackingen-abbey">Säckingen</a>, whose rights passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>. In 1352 the valley joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/confederate-states-of-america">Confederacy</a>, though on unequal terms. The Glarners' victory over a <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-habsburg">Habsburg</a> army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nafels">Näfels</a> in 1388, still commemorated each April, secured their independence, and they gained full equality with the other cantons in 1473.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">Sovereignty</a> lay with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landsgemeinde">Landsgemeinde</a>, the open-air assembly of all men, which still meets in Glarus. The valley lived from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> service and later textiles. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huldrych-zwingli">Huldrych Zwingli</a> was parish priest at Glarus before moving to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/canton-of-zurich">Zürich</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> divided the canton, and from 1623 Catholics and Protestants kept separate assemblies and officials alongside a common government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The old canton dissolved in 1798 under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/helvetic-republic">Helvetic Republic</a>, becoming part of the canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/linth">Linth</a>. Restored in 1803, Glarus remains a Swiss canton and one of two still governed by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landsgemeinde">Landsgemeinde</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/canton-of-glarus.jpg" alt="Canton of Glarus" width="320" height="389"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CHE_Kanton_Glarus_COA.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1352 CE – 1798 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Glarus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Reformed Protestantism, Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Swiss German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/switzerland">Switzerland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Glarus</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1575&amp;focus=canton-of-glarus" aria-label="Canton of Glarus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4893 526 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Canton of Glarus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5213 782L5186 782M5213 782L5188 772"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5186 782h0M5188 772h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5213 782h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5213 782h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Glarus. <a href="/atlas?year=1575&amp;focus=canton-of-glarus">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
